sequenceDiagram
    participant CM as CronManager (sibling pod)
    participant Gate as eFTI Gate (Ruuter ops route)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (via ReSql)

    Note over CM: Hourly at :45.<br/>Job efti_gate_expire_identifiers in<br/>DSL/CronManager/efti-ops.yaml.<br/>HTTP POST job → ops<br/>expire endpoint.

    CM->>+Gate: POST /ops/v1/expire-identifiers<br/>Authorization: Bearer ${ARCHIVE_OPS_TOKEN} (env OPS_AUTHORIZATION)
    Gate->>Gate: ops/.guard.yml: literal compare with ARCHIVE_OPS_TOKEN — 401 otherwise

    Gate->>+DB: expire_road_consignments (one statement):<br/>current rows (no newer sibling) with transport_mode='3',<br/>status='ACTIVE' and acceptance_date + 14 days < NOW(),<br/>oldest first, at most 1000
    Note over DB: Cabotage retention —<br/>Reg 2024/1942 Art 11(4).<br/>Latest-row resolution<br/>per db/README.md (ADR-009 anti-join).
    DB->>DB: INSERT a copy of each candidate with status='INACTIVE'<br/>(skipped when dryRun) — append-only, no UPDATE;<br/>the new row is the latest
    DB-->>-Gate: { candidateCount: 3, expiredCount: 3 }

    alt ReSql error
        Gate->>DB: insert_job_execution_log (job_name='expire-identifiers', status='FAILED')
        Gate-->>CM: 502 IDENTIFIER_EXPIRY_FAILED (CronManager retries)
    else dryRun: true
        Gate-->>CM: 200 { candidates: 3, expired: 0, dryRun: true, more: false }
    else sweep
        Gate->>+DB: insert_job_execution_log (job_name='expire-identifiers', status='COMPLETED',<br/>details: { candidates: 3, expired: 3, reason: "cabotage_14d" })
        DB-->>-Gate: ok
        Gate-->>-CM: 200 { candidates: 3, expired: 3, dryRun: false, more: false }
    end

    Note over CM: more: true (a full batch of 1000)<br/>is drained by the next hourly run.<br/>Non-road modes are NOT expired —<br/>cabotage rule applies to road only.<br/>Superseded ACTIVE rows are moved<br/>out by the archive sweep (Epic 26).
